nna  have the hard conversation with Bill  Belichick just my opinion because  Belichick will always do in my opinion I  think what is what's best for the team  overall and again now everything looks  you know swimming everything's wonderful  on the surface but Belichick is gonna  get to that point with Brady at some  point because I think we both feel that  Belichick is gonna coach well into the  future  and if he does that day is probably  going to come and we'll Tom Brady play  elsewhere  I believe if he has an opportunity to  play elsewhere and he really wants to  absolutely would he will not do in my  opinion if he's still healthy what Dan  Marino did when he almost went to  Minnesota but just said there's  something about playing your whole  career with one team I think Brady would  love to play his whole career with one  team but I think if he thinks he still  can play in the Patriots don't want him  he'll go to Team X and you know we  always assumed that above Bill Belichick  at the ownership level Robert Jonathan  Kraft that they that they are committed  to Tom Brady indefinitely but how can  you not look around the league right now  and see what this influx of young  quarterbacks is doing and look at how  Brady was knocked down statistically  relative to the top quarterbacks in the  game this year by these young guys and  not feel like we better get ours while  we can otherwise we're gonna get to a  point where we feel desperate to find a  quarterback and there's gonna be  franchise quarterbacks all throughout  the league and we're not gonna have one  if we just play this out until Tom Brady  leave so I agree with you there's an  urgency to find their young quarterback  who can become a great young quarterback  in the NFL after Tom Brady either walks  away or is not  hi I'm Mike Tirico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from NBC  Sports

